Feasibility review for cycle 004 is in `runs/Absolute_2026-09-28_02/decisions/cycle-004/review-feasibility.json`.

- **face_attached_depth.** Width and height are the factory face already on `EstimatePoseParams` (1.20 m by 0.14 m). The attached-depth window can run inside `estimate_pose_chamfer_v3_2` while the samples, the oriented plane, and `best_pose` are still local, using `project_points_to_plane_2d`, the inverse of `transform_points_2d`, and `point_to_plane_distance`. The outcome and `PalletPoseStamped` have no size fields, and `publish_pose` never sees those locals. An empty kept set has no seed, the proposal writes no flag and no substitute length, and a successful estimate still publishes `PalletPoseStamped`.
- **fork_opening_depth.** The two opening centres can be built from `±pocket_centre_offset_m` and lifted with `transform_points_2d`, `lift_point_from_plane_2d`, and `apply_se3` before return. Those maps are affine, so the mean of the two RGB z values is `pose.tz`, the face-centre range `publish_pose` already writes. The message has no centre fields.
- **published_face_sizes.** The estimator can copy the factory width and height and `centre_r.z()` onto the outcome before return. `depth_m` is that same optical z. `has_dimensions` is true on every published rich pose, because a failed estimate still publishes no `PalletPoseStamped`.
